t can be grumpy and uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). No info on decision speed.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), known to be 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere with crew (cooperation), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (crew), not willing to further education (adaptability). No stress resilience info.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as arrogant (crew), relatively weak leadership (crew), also arrogant may affect communication. No reliability info.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Candidate C has reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress resilience and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate A has strong technical and leadership but unorganized and poor at criticism. Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Possibly Candidate C: reliability, decision quality, crew positive, but communication issues could be mitigated? However egocentric and not willing to further education are concerns for adaptability. Candidate B: stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative and grumpy may affect crew. Candidate A: technical but unorganized and poor criticism acceptance may affect reliability. Candidate D: responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nI think Candidate C seems strongest on core safety criteria: reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere. Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe less than uncooperativeness or arrogance. So I will recommend Candidate C.\n\nNow produce public message: state recommendation, reference facts, explain why C is best, compare to others.\n\nProceed."}
